{"parentUuid":"ce573115-18b3-4599-8b87-e18b1ff01f0e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgBqRc8zqVuE43vmZmZHx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FokvyaMC9KpD14m3b2giE4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:/Users/YUNUS-~1/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit/07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f/scratchpad/m2_adr.py","content":"import subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\ndef edit(path, pairs):\n    p = Path(path)\n    s = p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    for old, new in pairs:\n        assert s.count(old) == 1, (path, old[:70], s.count(old))\n        s = s.replace(old, new)\n    p.write_text(s, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n\nedit(\"GUIDELINES.md\", [(\n    \"A file that parses but declares a version the reader does not support is refused in place: \"\n    \"it is never quarantined, overwritten or replaced by an older backup.\",\n    \"A file that parses but declares a version the reader does not support is refused in place: \"\n    \"it is never quarantined, overwritten or replaced by an older backup. A file the process \"\n    \"cannot read at all (locked, permission denied, unreadable device) has not failed to parse: \"\n    \"its content is unknown, so it is left in place and reported under R5, never quarantined.\")])\n\nedit(\"tests/test_kit.py\", [(\n    '                \"acquired with a 3-second timeout; a lock older than 30 seconds is broken\",\\n',\n    '                \"acquired with a 3-second timeout; a lock older than 30 seconds is broken\",\\n'\n    '                # ADR-146: an unreadable file is not a corrupt one.\\n'\n    '                \"A file the process cannot read at all (locked, permission denied, unreadable device) has \"\\n'\n    '                \"not failed to parse\",\\n')])\n\nciting = subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"scripts/sync_principles.py\", \"--citing\", \"PRINCIPLE-013\"],\n                        capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30, check=True).stdout.split()\nnotes = {\n    \"PRINCIPLE-013\": \"R4 adds the unreadable/unparseable distinction; R1's PermissionError-only retry is now obeyed by the code\",\n    \"PRINCIPLE-011\": \"R6 an unreadable ledger now ends with the triad through report_operational_error, not an empty ledger\",\n    \"PRINCIPLE-006\": \"a live task is no longer lost to a transient read failure; no conflict\",\n    \"PRINCIPLE-014\": \"R6 three failing-first tests pin both behaviours; no conflict\",\n    \"PRINCIPLE-000\": \"R5 a gate that reported success after losing data is the failure class this closes\",\n}\nparts = [f\"{pid} ({notes.get(pid, 'no conflict')})\" for pid in sorted(set(citing) | {\"PRINCIPLE-013\"})]\n\nadr = f\"\"\"\n### ADR-146: An Unreadable State File Is Reported, Not Quarantined; Only Lock Contention Is Retried\n- **Date**: 2026-10-19\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: Two defects where the code contradicted its own principle. (1) `load_ledger` caught `OSError` in the same handler as malformed JSON, so a ledger that was merely locked or permission-denied was renamed to `*.corrupt_*` and replaced by an older `.bak` or an empty ledger: a healthy file destroyed and the active task lost, on a fault that says nothing about the content. PRINCIPLE-013 R4 only ever authorised quarantining \"a file that does not parse\". (2) `atomic_write_json` retried `except (PermissionError, OSError)`, which collapses to `OSError`, so a full or read-only disk was retried five times with backoff before the identical failure surfaced, while PRINCIPLE-013 R1 says the retry is \"on `PermissionError`\".\n- **Decision**: `load_ledger` re-raises `OSError` from both the main file and the `.bak` recovery, so the CLI's `report_operational_error` prints the triad and exits 1 (PRINCIPLE-011 R6, PRINCIPLE-013 R5); quarantine and `.bak` recovery stay for `UnicodeDecodeError`, `json.JSONDecodeError` and `ValueError`, which are corruption. The `os.replace` loop catches `PermissionError` only. PRINCIPLE-013 R4 gains one clause: a file the process cannot read at all has not failed to parse, so it is left in place and reported under R5.\n- **Consequences**: A locked ledger now stops the command with a readable cause instead of silently starting an empty one. Pinned by `test_an_io_error_is_reported_not_quarantined`, `test_corruption_is_still_quarantined_and_recovered` and `test_replace_retries_lock_contention_but_not_a_full_disk`, all three failing first. The second was wrong on its first draft and taught something: `atomic_write_json` rotates a `.bak` only from an existing file, so a single write leaves no backup to recover from.\n- Cross-principle check: {\", \".join(parts)}.\n\"\"\"\nd = Path(\"knowledge/decisions.md\")\nd.write_text(d.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").rstrip(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\" + adr, encoding=\"utf-8\")\nprint(\"ok\", sorted(citing))\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":261,"cache_read_input_tokens":722408,"output_tokens":2587,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":215},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":261,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2587,"cache_read_input_tokens":722408,"cache_creation_input_tokens":261,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":261},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01FokvyaMC9KpD14m3b2giE4":{"file_path":"C:/Users/YUNUS-~1/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit/07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f/scratchpad/m2_adr.py","content":"import subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\ndef edit(path, pairs):\n    p = Path(path)\n    s = p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    for old, new in pairs:\n        assert s.count(old) == 1, (path, old[:70], s.count(old))\n        s = s.replace(old, new)\n    p.write_text(s, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n\nedit(\"GUIDELINES.md\", [(\n    \"A file that parses but declares a version the reader does not support is refused in place: \"\n    \"it is never quarantined, overwritten or replaced by an older backup.\",\n    \"A file that parses but declares a version the reader does not support is refused in place: \"\n    \"it is never quarantined, overwritten or replaced by an older backup. A file the process \"\n    \"cannot read at all (locked, permission denied, unreadable device) has not failed to parse: \"\n    \"its content is unknown, so it is left in place and reported under R5, never quarantined.\")])\n\nedit(\"tests/test_kit.py\", [(\n    '                \"acquired with a 3-second timeout; a lock older than 30 seconds is broken\",\\n',\n    '                \"acquired with a 3-second timeout; a lock older than 30 seconds is broken\",\\n'\n    '                # ADR-146: an unreadable file is not a corrupt one.\\n'\n    '                \"A file the process cannot read at all (locked, permission denied, unreadable device) has \"\\n'\n    '                \"not failed to parse\",\\n')])\n\nciting = subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"scripts/sync_principles.py\", \"--citing\", \"PRINCIPLE-013\"],\n                        capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30, check=True).stdout.split()\nnotes = {\n    \"PRINCIPLE-013\": \"R4 adds the unreadable/unparseable distinction; R1's PermissionError-only retry is now obeyed by the code\",\n    \"PRINCIPLE-011\": \"R6 an unreadable ledger now ends with the triad through report_operational_error, not an empty ledger\",\n    \"PRINCIPLE-006\": \"a live task is no longer lost to a transient read failure; no conflict\",\n    \"PRINCIPLE-014\": \"R6 three failing-first tests pin both behaviours; no conflict\",\n    \"PRINCIPLE-000\": \"R5 a gate that reported success after losing data is the failure class this closes\",\n}\nparts = [f\"{pid} ({notes.get(pid, 'no conflict')})\" for pid in sorted(set(citing) | {\"PRINCIPLE-013\"})]\n\nadr = f\"\"\"\n### ADR-146: An Unreadable State File Is Reported, Not Quarantined; Only Lock Contention Is Retried\n- **Date**: 2026-10-19\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: Two defects where the code contradicted its own principle. (1) `load_ledger` caught `OSError` in the same handler as malformed JSON, so a ledger that was merely locked or permission-denied was renamed to `*.corrupt_*` and replaced by an older `.bak` or an empty ledger: a healthy file destroyed and the active task lost, on a fault that says nothing about the content. PRINCIPLE-013 R4 only ever authorised quarantining \"a file that does not parse\". (2) `atomic_write_json` retried `except (PermissionError, OSError)`, which collapses to `OSError`, so a full or read-only disk was retried five times with backoff before the identical failure surfaced, while PRINCIPLE-013 R1 says the retry is \"on `PermissionError`\".\n- **Decision**: `load_ledger` re-raises `OSError` from both the main file and the `.bak` recovery, so the CLI's `report_operational_error` prints the triad and exits 1 (PRINCIPLE-011 R6, PRINCIPLE-013 R5); quarantine and `.bak` recovery stay for `UnicodeDecodeError`, `json.JSONDecodeError` and `ValueError`, which are corruption. The `os.replace` loop catches `PermissionError` only. PRINCIPLE-013 R4 gains one clause: a file the process cannot read at all has not failed to parse, so it is left in place and reported under R5.\n- **Consequences**: A locked ledger now stops the command with a readable cause instead of silently starting an empty one. Pinned by `test_an_io_error_is_reported_not_quarantined`, `test_corruption_is_still_quarantined_and_recovered` and `test_replace_retries_lock_contention_but_not_a_full_disk`, all three failing first. The second was wrong on its first draft and taught something: `atomic_write_json` rotates a `.bak` only from an existing file, so a single write leaves no backup to recover from.\n- Cross-principle check: {\", \".join(parts)}.\n\"\"\"\nd = Path(\"knowledge/decisions.md\")\nd.write_text(d.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").rstrip(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\" + adr, encoding=\"utf-8\")\nprint(\"ok\", sorted(citing))\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"293deacd-d3b8-4425-9c2b-c8eab8daf39d","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgBqRbjS8jrP3FmAUzB6V","requestRef":"7bf40dd7-1696-483c-aee3-19d0b1835adc","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1aa185ea-4568-4afa-92d2-347be74ca9ea","timestamp":"2026-10-19T15:31:15.222Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit","sessionId":"07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f","version":"2.1.302","gitBranch":"main","slug":"eager-humming-wave"}
