)\r"," \r"," **Classes:**\r"," - `class TestPrincipleSync` - *Verifies that all 20 principles are maintained and synchronized (PRINCIPLE-001, PRINCIPLE-017).*\r"]},{"oldStart":916,"oldLines":6,"newStart":916,"newLines":10,"lines":["   - Method `.test_unparseable_tier_output_fails_instead_of_reporting_zero()`\r","   - Method `.test_every_test_module_in_the_repository_has_a_budget()`\r","   - Method `.test_budget_errors_is_silent_when_every_tier_fits()`\r","+- `class TestChecklistWording` - *PRINCIPLE-000 R7 bans hedge words in \"every rule added or changed\", but the slices the*\r","+  - Method `.setUpClass()`\r","+  - Method `.test_checklists_contain_no_hedge_words()`\r","+  - Method `.test_every_checklist_item_cites_a_principle()`\r"," \r"," **Functions:**\r"," - `def _refuse_spawn(popen_self, args, *unused_args, **unused_kwargs)`\r"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\knowledge\\decisions.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1625,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1625,"newLines":11,"lines":[" - **Decision**: `load_ledger` re-raises `OSError` from both the main file and the `.bak` recovery, so the CLI's `report_operational_error` prints the triad and exits 1 (PRINCIPLE-011 R6, PRINCIPLE-013 R5); quarantine and `.bak` recovery stay for `UnicodeDecodeError`, `json.JSONDecodeError` and `ValueError`, which are corruption. The `os.replace` loop catches `PermissionError` only. PRINCIPLE-013 R4 gains one clause: a file the process cannot read at all has not failed to parse, so it is left in place and reported under R5.\r"," - **Consequences**: A locked ledger now stops the command with a readable cause instead of silently starting an empty one. Pinned by `test_an_io_error_is_reported_not_quarantined`, `test_corruption_is_still_quarantined_and_recovered` and `test_replace_retries_lock_contention_but_not_a_full_disk`, all three failing first. The second was wrong on its first draft and taught something: `atomic_write_json` rotates a `.bak` only from an existing file, so a single write leaves no backup to recover from.\r"," - Cross-principle check: PRINCIPLE-000 (R5 a gate that reported success after losing data is the failure class this closes), PRINCIPLE-006 (a live task is no longer lost to a transient read failure; no conflict), PRINCIPLE-007 (no conflict), PRINCIPLE-010 (no conflict), PRINCIPLE-011 (R6 an unreadable ledger now ends with the triad through report_operational_error, not an empty ledger), PRINCIPLE-013 (R4 adds the unreadable/unparseable distinction; R1's PermissionError-only retry is now obeyed by the code), PRINCIPLE-016 (no conflict), PRINCIPLE-017 (no conflict).\r","+\r","+### ADR-147: Three Gates Widened to the Rules They Serve\r","+- **Date**: 2026-10-19\r","+- **Status**: Accepted\r","+- **Context**: A verified review found three gates narrower than the rule each enforces. (1) The hygiene scan flagged only a broad `except` whose body is `pass`, so `except OSError: pass` — the commonest way a real failure is discarded — passed, and a test asserted that it must. Measured across this repository and the seven projects, the widened shape appears 14 times in `scripts/` and 43 times in `projects/`. (2) `audit_readme` validated `python scripts/<name>.py` and `python -m unittest tests.<module>` but not the 10 documented `python aikit.py <cmd>` commands, so a renamed subcommand could rot in the README. (3) PRINCIPLE-009 R5 bans assigning to another object's `_private` attribute and nothing checked it; ADR-082 left it ungated. Separately, PRINCIPLE-000 R7 bans hedge words in every rule, but the wording tests read only the principle sections, so the two checklists an agent runs carried \"concise\", \"dense\" and \"relevant\".\r","+- **Decision**: The hygiene scan flags any `except ...: pass` whatever it catches, and a broad handler (bare, `Exception`, `BaseException`) whose whole body is a lone `return`, `continue` or `break`; a typed handler that skips an item is a decision, not a silence. Each deliberate discard carries `hygiene: allow <reason>` on the handler's own line, and AIKit's own 13 legitimate sites now state their reason. `audit_readme` parses `scripts/aikit_cli.py` for `add_parser`/`project_command` names — parsed, never imported, because `aikit_cli` imports `update_knowledge_base` — and reports a documented subcommand the CLI does not declare. `audit_architecture` reports an assignment to `other._x` while leaving `self`/`cls` alone. The three hedging checklist items are reworded to name the limit they check, and `TestChecklistWording` extends R7's enforced slice to both checklists, also requiring each item to cite its principle.\r","+- **Consequences**: Widening (1) found a real defect in code committed one commit earlier: `load_ledger`'s missing-file branch still swallowed an I/O error on an existing `.bak` and started an empty ledger, the data-loss class ADR-146 closed on the other branch. It is fixed here. Assertion changed (PRINCIPLE-014 R2, under the user's instruction to fix): `test_startup_and_file_rules` required `except OSError: pass` to pass and no longer does; `test_any_handler_that_only_discards_is_flagged` replaces it and failed first. The projects' 43 sites are not touched here: each is a separate repository and its own `aikit check` now reports them. Still open in AIKit's own code: five pre-existing hygiene findings (four `open()` outside `with`, one untimed subprocess), left for their own task because the hygiene scan is a project gate and not part of AIKit's Phase 4.\r","+- Cross-principle check: none required; no principle section changed. The checklists and three gates serve PRINCIPLE-000 R5 and R7, PRINCIPLE-005 R3, PRINCIPLE-009 R5 and PRINCIPLE-014 R2.\r"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\knowledge\\services.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":6,"oldLines":14,"newStart":6,"newLines":14,"lines":[" | Service | Responsibility | Gate it provides |\r"," |---|---|---|\r"," | `sync_principles.py` | Generates every Tier 1 file in `TIER1_TARGETS` and README's principle table from `GUIDELINES.md`; computes `--involved` and `--citing` | `--check`: freshness, token budget, cross-principle ADR check (PRINCIPLE-000 R3) |\r","-| `update_knowledge_base.py` | Regenerates `codebase_map.md`; audits README, the ADR register, unfinished code and code structure | `--check` (PRINCIPLE-005, -007, -009 to -011, -016) |\r","+| `update_knowledge_base.py` | Regenerates `codebase_map.md`; audits README (including every `python aikit.py <cmd>` against the CLI's declared subcommands), the ADR register, unfinished code and code structure (including assignment to another object's `_private` attribute) | `--check` (PRINCIPLE-005, -007, -009 to -011, -016) |\r"," | `disruption_recovery.py` | Task ledger: checkpoints, resume, reset, track, commit-message validation; `--workspace <project>` uses that project's `.aikit/task_ledger.json` (ADR-120) | `--validate-commit`, `--track` (PRINCIPLE-002, -006) |\r"," | `check_reachability.py` | Finds production functions with no production caller and keys read but never written | exit 1 on either (PRINCIPLE-014 R7) |\r"," | `check_secrets.py` | Scans staged changes, tracked files and agent memory for credentials; `--workspace <dir>` scans that repository instead, e.g. a project (ADR-121) | exit 1 on a finding or an unscanned surface (PRINCIPLE-019) |\r"," | `aikit.py` (`aikit_cli.py`) | `new`, `attach`, `list`, `status`, `resume`, `checkpoint`, `complete`, `clean`, `guideline`, `check`, `fix`, `publish`, `delegate`: the projects AIKit builds, each its own folder and git repository (ADR-119) | exit 2 on a bad name or path, 1 on a failed request, with Why/Fix |\r"," | `project_registry.py` | Library behind `aikit.py`: finds projects, detects each one's stacks and test command (`DETECTORS`), writes `.aikit/project.json` and `.aikit/decisions.md` | none; reached through `aikit.py` |\r"," | `project_gates.py` | A project's gates: test command, extras detected from its config (`EXTRA_GATES`), `project.json` `gates` overrides, built-in hygiene scan, guidelines check and secret scan; runs them in the project folder | `python aikit.py check <name>` exits 1 on any failed gate or no test gate (ADR-122) |\r","-| `check_project_hygiene.py` | Scans a project's Python source and static assets: shell/system/exec, non-portable subprocess, unencoded `open()`, silent broad `except`, absolute paths, third-party asset URLs | exit 1 on a finding; built into `aikit check` (ADR-137) |\r","+| `check_project_hygiene.py` | Scans a project's Python source and static assets: shell/system/exec, non-portable subprocess, unencoded `open()`, any `except` that only discards the error, absolute paths, third-party asset URLs | exit 1 on a finding; built into `aikit check` (ADR-137) |\r"," | `project_publish.py` | Uploads a project's commits to its own GitHub repository (`gh repo create --private --source --remote origin --push`, or a push to an existing `origin`) and auto-pushes after a passing `aikit check`; both first scan exactly the commits they push (`check_secrets.py --commits`: the whole history for a new remote, `@{u}..HEAD` after) and refuse on a finding | `aikit publish` exits 1 on a refusal (ADR-134, ADR-145) |\r"," | `subagent_delegate.py` | Runs one OpenCode sub-agent (roles = `.opencode/agents/*.md`) supervised, stdin closed, with a timeout; reports a ledger changed during the run | `aikit delegate` exits 1 on timeout or a changed ledger (ADR-128) |\r"," | `dogfood.py` | Runs AIKit's CLIs as real processes in a sandbox: golden path, chaos, gates, `--help` budget | exit 1 on any failed track (PRINCIPLE-015) |"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\knowledge\\codebase_map.md","C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\knowledge\\decisions.md","C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\knowledge\\services.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"19d7936b-3169-4034-bfaa-3d0a8688f89e","c