{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"a7f18ecc-6f03-4638-ae8e-634764ac276c","snapshotMessageId":"e4b36592-c38d-4157-9271-6f6babcf63a8","trackingPath":"C:\\Users\\YUNUS-~1\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit\\07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f\\scratchpad\\m4_adr.py","backup":{"backupFileName":null,"version":1,"backupTime":"2026-10-19T15:41:12.915Z","realParentDir":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit\\07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f\\scratchpad"},"timestamp":"2026-10-19T15:41:12.915Z"}
{"parentUuid":"f781817f-b4f1-4d15-a75b-f65d64025799","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgBrCfLjf7h2guWCztkAu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E8pBiJwyvMamenFBLNYeo8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:/Users/YUNUS-~1/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit/07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f/scratchpad/m4_adr.py","content":"from pathlib import Path\n\nadr = \"\"\"\n### ADR-148: Chaos Coverage Names Its Tests, and the Full-Disk Path Is Driven\n- **Date**: 2026-10-19\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: PRINCIPLE-013 R7 asks for a test per named fault, and `TestChaosCoverage` checked that by matching test *names* against regexes (`bak|shadow`, `malformed|corrupt`, `headroom|disk_space|enospc`). Any name containing those letters satisfied it, so renaming or deleting the real test left a fault silently uncovered, and the gate could pass with no behavioural test behind it. The disk-space entry was satisfied by `test_disk_headroom_check`, which called `check_disk_headroom()` and asserted its boolean: nothing ever drove a write under a full disk, so the refusal path, the surviving previous state and the triad were untested.\n- **Decision**: `TestChaosCoverage.FAULTS` maps each fault to the exact test name that drives it, and the test asserts that name exists; two faults the review exposed are added, `unreadable state file` and `failed rename` (ADR-146). `test_a_full_disk_refuses_the_write_and_keeps_the_old_state` patches `shutil.disk_usage` to report 1 KiB free, drives `atomic_write_json`, and asserts ENOSPC, the headroom warning, the previous bytes intact, no `*.tmp_*` left, and that `report_operational_error` turns it into PRINCIPLE-011 R6's triad.\n- **Consequences**: Both were verified to bite: with the headroom guard stubbed out the disk test fails, and with one fault's name changed the coverage test fails. A renamed chaos test now breaks the build instead of passing by accident.\n- Cross-principle check: none required; no principle section changed. Serves PRINCIPLE-013 R2/R7, PRINCIPLE-011 R6 and PRINCIPLE-014 R5.\n\"\"\"\np = Path(\"knowledge/decisions.md\")\np.write_text(p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").rstrip(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\" + adr, encoding=\"utf-8\")\nprint(\"ok\")\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":538,"cache_read_input_tokens":774145,"output_tokens":1249,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":538,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1249,"cache_read_input_tokens":774145,"cache_creation_input_tokens":538,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":538},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01E8pBiJwyvMamenFBLNYeo8":{"file_path":"C:/Users/YUNUS-~1/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit/07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f/scratchpad/m4_adr.py","content":"from pathlib import Path\n\nadr = \"\"\"\n### ADR-148: Chaos Coverage Names Its Tests, and the Full-Disk Path Is Driven\n- **Date**: 2026-10-19\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: PRINCIPLE-013 R7 asks for a test per named fault, and `TestChaosCoverage` checked that by matching test *names* against regexes (`bak|shadow`, `malformed|corrupt`, `headroom|disk_space|enospc`). Any name containing those letters satisfied it, so renaming or deleting the real test left a fault silently uncovered, and the gate could pass with no behavioural test behind it. The disk-space entry was satisfied by `test_disk_headroom_check`, which called `check_disk_headroom()` and asserted its boolean: nothing ever drove a write under a full disk, so the refusal path, the surviving previous state and the triad were untested.\n- **Decision**: `TestChaosCoverage.FAULTS` maps each fault to the exact test name that drives it, and the test asserts that name exists; two faults the review exposed are added, `unreadable state file` and `failed rename` (ADR-146). `test_a_full_disk_refuses_the_write_and_keeps_the_old_state` patches `shutil.disk_usage` to report 1 KiB free, drives `atomic_write_json`, and asserts ENOSPC, the headroom warning, the previous bytes intact, no `*.tmp_*` left, and that `report_operational_error` turns it into PRINCIPLE-011 R6's triad.\n- **Consequences**: Both were verified to bite: with the headroom guard stubbed out the disk test fails, and with one fault's name changed the coverage test fails. A renamed chaos test now breaks the build instead of passing by accident.\n- Cross-principle check: none required; no principle section changed. Serves PRINCIPLE-013 R2/R7, PRINCIPLE-011 R6 and PRINCIPLE-014 R5.\n\"\"\"\np = Path(\"knowledge/decisions.md\")\np.write_text(p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").rstrip(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\" + adr, encoding=\"utf-8\")\nprint(\"ok\")\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"58055d85-7e65-481e-a53f-5fe7d8429a9a","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgBrCeWt7cHGg5NZbmuup","requestRef":"d43e1258-de54-415b-aa4f-f645950adfab","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a7f18ecc-6f03-4638-ae8e-634764ac276c","timestamp":"2026-10-19T15:41:12.833Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit","sessionId":"07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f","version":"2.1.302","gitBranch":"main","slug":"eager-humming-wave"}
