{"parentUuid":"5d072b12-86aa-45ce-af3b-c933de238b31","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgBrDsYizs4uGnp3KdfLY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NN8ZGw6o2ogUEpJfihNmjK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"MSG=\"test(chaos): [milestone 4/5] name each fault's test, drive a full disk\"; py scripts/disruption_recovery.py --validate-commit \"$MSG\" && py scripts/disruption_recovery.py --checkpoint review-fixes-2 --phase-num 5 --desc \"[milestone 4/5] committed: exact-name chaos map, behavioural full-disk test (ADR-148)\" | tail -1 && git add .agents/task_ledger.json knowledge/codebase_map.md knowledge/decisions.md tests/test_kit.py 2>&1 | grep -v \"LF will\"; py scripts/check_secrets.py --staged >/dev/null 2>&1 && test -z \"$(git status --short | grep -v '^[AM] ')\" && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF' && git push -q && git log --oneline -1\ntest(chaos): [milestone 4/5] name each fault's test, drive a full disk\n\nPRINCIPLE-013 R7's coverage gate matched test *names* against regexes,\nso any name containing \"bak\" or \"corrupt\" satisfied it and a renamed\ntest left the fault silently uncovered. The map now holds exact test\nnames, with two faults the review exposed added. The disk-space entry\nwas satisfied by a test that only called check_disk_headroom(); a new\ntest drives a write under a 1 KiB disk and asserts ENOSPC, the warning,\nthe previous state intact, no partial buffer, and the triad. Both were\nverified to fail when their subject is removed (ADR-148).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF","description":"Commit and push milestone 4","timeout":200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1530,"cache_read_input_tokens":774683,"output_tokens":682,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_f