{"parentUuid":"1024d9b8-d123-4e68-8268-73cb3b7763a2","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01DXV8DCuryPo4r6s49w1ow4","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"bea524d7-4279-42c9-8de4-b6985f3899eb","timestamp":"2026-10-19T15:42:27.801Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit","sessionId":"07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f","version":"2.1.302","gitBranch":"main","slug":"eager-humming-wave"}
{"parentUuid":"bea524d7-4279-42c9-8de4-b6985f3899eb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgBrHpN6cfM7JAENNiNnf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All five milestones are committed and pushed, the tree is clean, and every gate passes (unit 3.9–4.1ms/test against an 8ms ceiling, integration 176ms against 200ms, all five read-only gates green).\n\n**What got fixed**\n\n| Commit | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| `9eaaace` | `check_secrets.py --commits <range>`; `publish` and the auto-push now scan **the commits they upload**, not the working tree. Scanning the tree let a key that was committed then deleted in an uncommitted edit through. Also fixed the stale \"six Tier 1 files\" line I'd reported. |\n| `7e4a939` | A ledger that was merely **locked or permission-denied** was renamed to `*.corrupt_*` and replaced by an empty one — a healthy file destroyed and the live task lost. It now raises and the CLI prints the triad. `os.replace` retries `PermissionError` only, as PRINCIPLE-013 R1 already required. |\n| `b6e5465` | Three gates widened to the rules they serve: any `except …: pass` (not just broad ones), README parity for all 10 `python aikit.py` commands, and PRINCIPLE-009 R5's private-attribute ban. Checklists lost the hedge words R7 bans, now covered by a test. |\n| `080f364` | Chaos coverage keyed to **exact test names** instead of regexes that any name containing \"bak\" satisfied, plus a real full-disk test that drives a write and asserts ENOSPC, intact prior state, no partial buffer, and the triad. |\n\n**Two things worth your attention**\n\n1. **The widened gate immediately caught a real bug in the commit before it.** `load_ledger`'s missing-file branch still swallowed an I/O error on an existing `.bak` and started an empty ledger — the same data-loss class I'd just fixed on the other branch, one code path over. That's the gate paying for itself within minutes.\n2. **I started by making a mistake and had to recover.** There was an in-progress task, `review-fixes-2`, with uncommitted work in the tree. My first checkpoint superseded it before I checked — exactly what PRINCIPLE-006 tells an agent not to do. `--resume` caught it, I restored the task, read every line of the work in flight, and verified it before committing. The work was another session's; I didn't write it, and I've said so in each commit's provenance.\n\n**Still open, deliberately**\n\n- **43 silent-except findings across the 7 projects.** Each is its own git repository, so sweeping them is 7 more commits. Their own `aikit check` now reports them.\n- **5 pre-existing findings in AIKit's own code** (4 `open()` outside `with`, 1 untimed subprocess). Left alone because they predate this work and because the hygiene gate is a *project* gate — it isn't in AIKit's own Phase 4 list at all, which is itself a scope question.\n- **The two big items from my proposal I did not touch:** labelling each of the 136 rules `universal` vs `kit`, and giving projects the reachability/dogfood/persistence gates. Those change what every project must pass, so I'd want your decision first.\n- **The project code-quality audit** you asked for. I read \"fix\" as *do the work*, so I went at the confirmed defects instead. The audit is still worth doing and would tell us which of the remaining gaps actually bite in your 31,000 lines.\n\nWhich of those three do you want next?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":523,"cache_read_input_tokens":778137,"output_tokens":1139,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":523,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1139,"cache_read_input_tokens":778137,"cache_creation_input_tokens":523,"cache