tId":"req_011CgBrPJzgME97ti9rxdUsv","requestRef":"ed827a7e-4d50-4154-b8ec-09ab8d333b51","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"741f8cfc-e9d9-4209-8395-e15448ebc935","timestamp":"2026-10-19T15:43:39.274Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit","sessionId":"07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f","version":"2.1.302","gitBranch":"main","slug":"eager-humming-wave"}
{"parentUuid":"741f8cfc-e9d9-4209-8395-e15448ebc935","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c3602802-0490-4257-a831-b5d201a35c9d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0161DcwaGGtXGCy2tZFvUy44","type":"tool_result","content":"### ADR-142: Delivery Checks Verify the Committed Tree, Not Just a Dirty Working Copy\n- **Date**: 2026-10-19\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: `aikit check` ran a project's gates against the working tree and then auto-pushed existing commits. A project could therefore pass with uncommitted fixes while the pushed commit was older and unverified; CyberPulse's completed ledger task demonstrated exactly that. Separately, the generated project README fell back to `python aikit.py check <name>` as the canonical gate, which cannot run from a project checked out without the AIKit workspace.\n- **Decision**: Add `aikit check --strict`: it requires a git repository, no uncommitted non-bookkeeping changes, and a `.aikit/codebase_map.md` when Python sources exist. It fails with the triad and pushes nothing. Ordinary `check` keeps its gate behavior but warns on baseline gaps and skips auto-push when the tree is dirty. Generated READMEs use the project's detected test command, or a `<FILL: ...>` placeholder when none exists, never the AIKit CLI as the project's canonical gate.\n- **Consequences**: Delivery can run `check --strict` in CI or before a release and know the pushed commit is the tested one. Existing projects without a map or with dirty work need a commit plus `aikit fix` before strict passes. The project README template now describes project commands rather than AIKit's own scripts.\n- Cross-principle check: none required; no principle text changed. Serves PRINCIPLE-005 (cold-start README), PRINCIPLE-011 R8 (project workspace), PRINCIPLE-014 (verified tests) and PRINCIPLE-018 (push only verified work).\n\n== P018 rules\n  1. **Automatic Conventional Commits**\n  2. **Explicit Staging Invariant (Zero Blind Staging)**\n  3. **Pre-Commit Delivery Triad Gate**\n  4. **Adaptive Push & Zero Force Push**\n  5. **Non-Destructive Recoil Invariant**\n  6. **Terse Delivery Confirmation**","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2bf3be05-1f34-479b-827c-d223a4f1c058","timestamp":"2026-10-19T15:43:40.055Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"### ADR-142: Delivery Checks Verify the Committed Tree, Not Just a Dirty Working Copy\n- **Date**: 2026-10-19\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: `aikit check` ran a project's gates against the working tree and then auto-pushed existing commits. A project could therefore pass with uncommitted fixes while the pushed commit was older and unverified; CyberPulse's completed ledger task demonstrated exactly that. Separately, the generated project README fell back to `python aikit.py check <name>` as the canonical gate, which cannot run from a project checked out without the AIKit workspace.\n- **Decision**: Add `aikit check --strict`: it requires a git repository, no uncommitted non-bookkeeping changes, and a `.aikit/codebase_map.md` when Python sources exist. It fails with the triad and pushes nothing. Ordinary `check` keeps its gate behavior but warns on baseline gaps and skips auto-push when the tree is dirty. Generated READMEs use the project's detected test command, or a `<FILL: ...>` placeholder when none exists, never the AIKit CLI as the project's canonical gate.\n- **Consequences**: Delivery can run `check --strict` in CI or before a release and know the pushed commit is the tested one. Existing projects without a map or with dirty work need a commit plus `aikit fix` before strict passes. The project README template now describes project commands rather than AIKit's own scripts.\n- Cross-principle check: none required; no principle text changed. Serves PRINCIPLE-005 (cold-start README), PRINCIPLE-011 R8 (project workspace), PRINCIPLE-014 (verified tests) and PRINCIPLE-018 (push only verified work).\n\n== P018 rules\n  1. **Automatic Conventional Commits**\n  2. **Explicit Staging Invariant (Zero Blind Staging)**\n  3. **Pre-Commit Delivery Triad Gate**\n  4. **Adaptive Push & Zero Force Push**\n  5. **Non-Destructive Recoil Invariant**\n  6. **Terse Delivery Confirmation**","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"f9e4e005-44b1-4348-9dab-e7c1878cf95e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit","root":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Aegean-E/AIKit","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Aegean-E/AIKit","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Aegean-E/AIKit","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"741f8cfc-e9d9-4209-8395-e15448ebc935","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit","sessionId":"07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f","version":"2.1.302","gitBranch":"main","slug":"eager-humming-wave"}
