{"parentUuid":"850890a2-dd1a-4841-b1d3-ca49a0672391","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c3602802-0490-4257-a831-b5d201a35c9d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BpMhi4MvZTmfi7eZZwjMNs","type":"tool_result","content":"  4. **Adaptive Push & Zero Force Push** *[Agent]*: After a commit the agent pushes to the current branch's upstream, unless the user said not to push. A branch without an upstream is pushed with `git push -u origin <branch>` when a remote named `origin` exists; with no remote it reports the commit as local only, and with remotes but none named `origin` it asks the user which to use. When the push is rejected because the remote moved, it runs `git pull --rebase` and pushes again; when the rebase stops on a conflict, it runs `git rebase --abort` and asks the user (PRINCIPLE-003 R6). It MUST NOT run `git push --force` or `--force-with\n  5. **Non-Destructive Recoil Invariant** *[Agent]*: To undo its own commit that is not yet pushed, the agent runs `git reset --soft HEAD^` (the parent commit); to undo a pushed commit, `git revert <hash>`. It MUST NOT run `git reset --hard`, `git clean`, `git checkout -- <file>`, `git restore <file>` or `git stash drop` on changes it did not make in this task.\n  6. **Terse Delivery Confirmation** *[Agent]*: The final message names, for every commit made, its short hash (`git rev-parse --short HEAD`), its subject, the number of files and the branch, and says whether it was pushed.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4d830851-3733-4122-b86c-5aec38159648","timestamp":"2026-10-19T15:44:04.154Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"  4. **Adaptive Push & Zero Force Push** *[Agent]*: After a commit the agent pushes to the current branch's upstream, unless the user said not to push. A branch without an upstream is pushed with `git push -u origin <branch>` when a remote named `origin` exists; with no remote it reports the commit as local only, and with remotes but none named `origin` it asks the user which to use. When the push is rejected because the remote moved, it runs `git pull --rebase` and pushes again; when the rebase stops on a conflict, it runs `git rebase --abort` and asks the user (PRINCIPLE-003 R6). It MUST NOT run `git push --force` or `--force-with\n  5. **Non-Destructive Recoil Invariant** *[Agent]*: To undo its own commit that is not yet pushed, the agent runs `git reset --soft HEAD^` (the parent commit); to undo a pushed commit, `git revert <hash>`. It MUST NOT run `git reset --hard`, `git clean`, `git checkout -- <file>`, `git restore <file>` or `git stash drop` on changes it did not make in this task.\n  6. **Terse Delivery Confirmation** *[Agent]*: The final message names, for every commit made, its short hash (`git rev-parse --short HEAD`), its subject, the number of files and the branch, and says whether it was pushed.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"c5b596b0-d731-4c7c-a0e8-c1bddd8a064b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit","root":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Aegean-E/AIKit","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Aegean-E/AIKit","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Aegean-E/AIKit","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"850890a2-dd1a-4841-b1d3-ca49a0672391","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit","sessionId":"07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5