 \"2026-10-19 18:42:02\"\r","+    },\r","+    {\r","+      \"task_id\": \"post-commit-verify\",\r","+      \"phase\": \"in_progress\",\r","+      \"phase_num\": 2,\r","+      \"description\": \"[1/2] scripts/verify_commit.py: throwaway worktree at the ref, full gate set inside it, secrets over the unpushed range, RAII removal, terse report, exit 0/1/2; unit tests with an injected runner; [2/2] PRINCIPLE-018 R7 verify-before-push, docs, ADR-149\",\r","+      \"files_affected\": [],\r","+      \"status\": \"in_progress\",\r","+      \"timestamp\": 1792424680.282783,\r","+      \"timestamp_str\": \"2026-10-19 18:44:40\",\r","+      \"impact_assessment\": {\r","+        \"why\": \"the pre-commit triad runs on the working tree, so a commit can contain less than what was tested: ADR-145 was committed without its implementation and a stale codebase map was committed twice today\",\r","+        \"benefits\": \"a broken commit is caught while it is still local, where PRINCIPLE-018 R5 undoes it with reset --soft instead of a revert, and the pushed history stays green for bisect and for anyone who checks out that commit\",\r","+        \"risks\": \"contract: new script and a new P018 rule; dependency: git worktree (already used by the kit's own tooling); concurrency: the worktree lives in the system temp dir, never inside the repository; state: none, the worktree is removed in a finally block\",\r","+        \"mitigation\": \"runner injected so unit tests spawn nothing; worktree removed even when a gate fails; one real end-to-end run recorded as evidence; integration test kept to the --help contract so the tier ceiling holds\"\r","+      }\r","+    },\r","+    {\r","+      \"task_id\": \"post-commit-verify\",\r","+      \"phase\": \"in_progress\",\r","+      \"phase_num\": 3,\r","+      \"description\": \"implementing [1/2]\",\r","+      \"files_affected\": [],\r","+      \"status\": \"in_progress\",\r","+      \"timestamp\": 1792424680.4567282,\r","+      \"timestamp_str\": \