{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f","hash":"1743bbeaca15418a031fbc0a3796759e6bc0b38a6f8c216a62681e792cecd776","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Design: commit → verify **HEAD in a throwaway worktree** → push only if green. Catching it while the commit is still local means recovery is `git reset --soft HEAD^` (P018 R5) instead of a revert. Recording the plan:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UzHaW6FUDphQPsK4pdGcQ8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit && py scripts/disruption_recovery.py --checkpoint post-commit-verify --phase-num 2 --desc \"[1/2] scripts/verify_commit.py: throwaway worktree at the ref, full gate set inside it, secrets over the unpushed range, RAII removal, terse report, exit 0/1/2; unit tests with an injected runner; [2/2] PRINCIPLE-018 R7 verify-before-push, docs, ADR-149\" --why \"the pre-commit triad runs on the working tree, so a commit can contain less than what was tested: ADR-145 was committed without its implementation and a stale codebase map was committed twice today\" --benefits \"a broken commit is caught while it is still local, where PRINCIPLE-018 R5 undoes it with reset --soft instead of a revert, and the pushed history stays green for bisect and for anyone who checks out that commit\" --risks \"contract: new script and a new P018 rule; dependency: git worktree (already used by the kit's own tooling); concurrency: the worktree lives in the system temp dir, never inside the repository; state: none, the worktree is removed in a finally block\" --mitigation \"runner injected so unit tests spawn nothing; worktree removed even when a gate fails; one real end-to-end run recorded as evidence; integration test kept to the --help contract so the tier ceiling holds\" | tail -1; py scripts/disruption_recovery.py --checkpoint post-commit-verify --phase-num 3 --desc \"implementing [1/2]\" | tail -1","description":"Record plan with impact assessment"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
