&1 | grep -E \"PASS|FAIL|OK\\]\"","description":"Add R7, pin, docs, ADR-149; sync and run tiers","timeout":600000}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_017yeac9eJnVmWzUiTLw5fXN":{"cwd":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"716bab15-b9a8-4f8f-bdc3-708e21d2256e","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgBroU2KenChP94ynPN3F","requestRef":"63caa232-b0a3-46c1-af90-92a8f3cf228a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ae738072-b177-473b-8e00-23cbd1053625","timestamp":"2026-10-19T15:49:24.992Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit","sessionId":"07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f","version":"2.1.302","gitBranch":"main","slug":"eager-humming-wave"}
{"parentUuid":"ae738072-b177-473b-8e00-23cbd1053625","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c3602802-0490-4257-a831-b5d201a35c9d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017yeac9eJnVmWzUiTLw5fXN","type":"tool_result","content":"ok ['PRINCIPLE-001', 'PRINCIPLE-002', 'PRINCIPLE-003', 'PRINCIPLE-006', 'PRINCIPLE-007', 'PRINCIPLE-008', 'PRINCIPLE-010', 'PRINCIPLE-011', 'PRINCIPLE-015', 'PRINCIPLE-016', 'PRINCIPLE-017', 'PRINCIPLE-019']\r\n[ERROR] 8 target(s) breach the Tier 1 context budget (PRINCIPLE-001).\n[TIER 1B HEADROOM] AGENTS.md: ~1304 tokens leaves room for only ~285 of the promised ~300 Tier 1B tokens\n[TIER 1B HEADROOM] GEMINI.md: ~1304 tokens leaves room for only ~284 of the promised ~300 Tier 1B tokens\n[TIER 1B HEADROOM] principles.md: ~1304 tokens leaves room for only ~284 of the promised ~300 Tier 1B tokens\n[FAIL] tests.test_kit: 341 tests in 1.518s = 4.45ms per test (ceiling 8.00ms)\n[FAIL] tests.test_integration: 45 tests in 8.047s = 178.82ms per test (ceiling 200.00ms)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0b94ff0d-3a5f-478d-9e38-09679228b2fb","timestamp":"2026-10-19T15:49:37.696Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"ok ['PRINCIPLE-001', 'PRINCIPLE-002', 'PRINCIPLE-003', 'PRINCIPLE-006', 'PRINCIPLE-007', 'PRINCIPLE-008', 'PRINCIPLE-010', 'PRINCIPLE-011', 'PRINCIPLE-015', 'PRINCIPLE-016', 'PRINCIPLE-017', 'PRINCIPLE-019']\r\n[ERROR] 8 target(s) breach the Tier 1 context budget (PRINCIPLE-001).\n[TIER 1B HEADROOM] AGENTS.md: ~1304 tokens leaves room for only ~285 of the promised ~300 Tier 1B tokens\n[TIER 1B HEADROOM] GEMINI.md: ~1304 tokens leaves room for only ~284 of the promised ~300 Tier 1B tokens\n[TIER 1B HEADROOM] principles.md: ~1304 tokens leaves room for only ~284 of the promised ~300 Tier 1B tokens\n[FAIL] tests.test_kit: 341 tests in 1.518s = 4.45ms per test (ceiling 8.00ms)\n[FAIL] tests.test_integration: 45 tests in 8.047s = 178.82ms per test (ceiling 200.00ms)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\GUIDELINES.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":315,"oldLines":7,"newStart":315,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ### PRINCIPLE-018: Automatic Git Workflow (Commit & Push)\r"," - **Problem**: Uncommitted work is lost; blind staging sweeps secrets and clutter into commits; diverged remotes tempt force-pushes; destructive resets erase work. When the rules claim a lock that does not exist, list only some blind-staging forms or give one rollback for every case, each model takes different risks with the user's history.\r"," - **Concept**: The agent commits each verified unit of work with a checked message, stages files by name, pushes without force, and undoes mistakes without discarding anything. The gates are enforced by the agent running them, not by a hook.\r","-- **Invariant**: Automatic conventional commits (`--validate-commit`) + adaptive push, unless the user opts out, never forced; explicit staging (zero `git add .`); pre-commit delivery triad (tests, read-only gates, staged diff); non-destructive recoil.\r","+- **Invariant**: Automatic conventional commits (`--validate-commit`) + adaptive push, unless the user opts out, never forced; explicit staging (zero `git add .`); pre-commit delivery triad (tests, read-only gates, staged diff); the commit itself verified before the push (`verify_commit.py`); non-destructive recoil.\r"," - **Rules**:\r","   1. **Automatic Conventional Commits** *[Agent]*: When Phase 4 passes for a milestone or a task (PRINCIPLE-006 R1), the agent commits, unless the user said not to commit; then it stops after Phase 4 and reports the uncommitted files. The subject is `type(scope): description` or `type(scope): [milestone N/M] description`, with a type from `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `docs`, `chore`, `test`, `perf`, `build`, `ci`, and at most 72 characters; `python scripts/disruption_recovery.py --validate-commit \"<message>\"` MUST pass before the commit.\r","   2. **Explicit Staging Invariant (Zero Blind Staging)** *[Agent]*: The agent stages files only by name (`git add <file> ...`). It MUST NOT run `git add .`, `git add -A`, `git add --all`, `git add -u` or `git commit -a`.\r"]},{"oldStart":323,"oldLines":6,"newStart":323,"newLines":7,"lines":["   4. **Adaptive Push & Zero Force Push** *[Agent]*: After a commit the agent pushes to the current branch's upstream, unless the user said not to push. A branch without an upstream is pushed with `git push -u origin <branch>` when a remote named `origin` exists; with no remote it reports the commit as local only, and with remotes but none named `origin` it asks the user which to use. When the push is rejected because the remote moved, it runs `git pull --rebase` and pushes again; when the rebase stops on a conflict, it runs `git rebase --abort` and asks the user (PRINCIPLE-003 R6). It MUST NOT run `git push --force` or `--force-with-lease` unless the user asked for that push.\r","   5. **Non-Destructive Recoil Invariant** *[Agent]*: To undo its own commit that is not yet pushed, the agent runs `git reset --soft HEAD^` (the parent commit); to undo a pushed commit, `git revert <hash>`. It MUST NOT run `git reset --hard`, `git clean`, `git checkout -- <file>`, `git restore <file>` or `git stash drop` on changes it did not make in this task.\r","   6. **Terse Delivery Confirmation** *[Agent]*: The final message names, for every commit made, its short hash (`git rev-parse --short HEAD`), its subject, the number of files and the branch, and says whether it was pushed.\r","+  7. **Post-Commit Verification of the Delivered Commit** *[Agent]*: After each commit, and before R4's push, the agent runs `python scripts/verify_commit.py`; the push follows only when it exits 0. It checks the commit out into a throwaway worktree and runs R3's gates against that commit alone, because R3 proves the working tree is green and the commit is a different tree whenever staging is a subset of it (R2). On a failure the agent undoes the still-unpushed commit with R5's `git reset --soft HEAD^`, adds what the commit lacked, and commits again. A project's commits are verified by `python aikit.py check --strict <name>` instead (PRINCIPLE-011 R8).\r"," \r"," ---\r"," \r"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":38,"oldLines":6,"newStart":38,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | **Reset Active Task**        | `python scripts/disruption_recovery.py --reset [reason]` | Abandons/clears in-progress task in ledger |\r"," | **Purge Temp Buffers**       | `python scripts/disruption_recovery.py --clean` | Deletes orphaned `*.tmp_*` buffers older than 60 s; younger ones may be a write in progress |\r"," | **Secret Scan Gate** | `python scripts/check_secrets.py --staged\\|--commits <range> [--workspace <project>]` | Exits 1 on a credential pattern in the staged diff or agent memory, or when any surface could not be scanned (PRINCIPLE-019) |\r","+| **Verify the Commit Itself** | `python scripts/verify_commit.py` | Runs every gate against the commit alone in a throwaway worktree; exits 1 when the commit holds less than the tree it was tested in (PRINCIPLE-018 R7) |\r"," | **Reachability Shield** | `python scripts/check_reachability.py` | No unwired capability or phantom state key (PRINCIPLE-014 R7) |\r"," | **Operational Dogfood Gate** | `python scripts/dogfood.py` | 5/5 tracks pass; zero host mutation (PRINCIPLE-015) |\r"," | **Discover Any CLI** | `python scripts/<script>.py --help` | Prints usage and exits `0` in <200ms as a fresh process, writing nothing |\r"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\knowledge\\codebase_map.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":10,"oldLines":7,"newStart":10,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - **Total Classes**: `77`\r"," - **Total Top-Level Functions**: `241`\r"," - **Total Class Methods**: `452`\r","-- **Total Source Lines**: `12840`\r","+- **Total Source Lines**: `12843`\r"," \r"," ---\r"," \r"]},{"oldStart":505,"oldLines":7,"newStart":505,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ### [`tests/test_kit.py`](tests/test_kit.py)\r"," > *Automated Test Suite for Portable Agent Kit (PRINCIPLE-011, PRINCIPLE-016)*\r"," \r","-**Size**: `4978` lines (`277220` bytes)\r","+**Size**: `4981` lines (`277494` bytes)\r"," \r"," **Classes:**\r"," - `class TestPrincipleSync` - *Verifies that all 20 principles are maintained and synchronized (PRINCIPLE-001, PRINCIPLE-017).*\r"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\knowledge\\decisions.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1641,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1641,"newLines":11,"lines":[" - **Decision**: `TestChaosCoverage.FAULTS` maps each fault to the exact test name that drives it, and the test asserts that name exists; two faults the review exposed are added, `unreadable state file` and `failed rename` (ADR-146). `test_a_full_disk_refuses_the_write_and_keeps_the_old_state` patches `shutil.disk_usage` to report 1 KiB free, drives `atomic_write_json`, and asserts ENOSPC, the headroom warning, the previous bytes intact, no `*.tmp_*` left, and that `report_operational_error` turns it into PRINCIPLE-011 R6's triad.\r"," - **Consequences**: Both were verified to bite: with the headroom guard stubbed out the disk test fails, and with one fault's name changed the coverage test fails. A renamed chaos test now breaks the build instead of passing by accident.\r"," - Cross-principle check: none required; no principle section changed. Serves PRINCIPLE-013 R2/R7, PRINCIPLE-011 R6 and PRINCIPLE-014 R5.\r","+\r","+### ADR-149: The Commit Is Verified On Its Own Before It Is Pushed\r","+- **Date**: 2026-10-19\r","+- **Status**: Accepted\r","+- **Context**: PRINCIPLE-018 R3 runs the delivery triad against the working tree. Under R2's explicit staging the commit is a *different* tree whenever staging is a subset, and nothing checked that one. Both failure modes happened on 2026-10-19: ADR-145 was committed while its implementation sat unstaged, and a stale `codebase_map.md` was committed twice, each time caught only by the next run. Projects already had `aikit check --strict` (ADR-142); AIKit's own commits had no equivalent.\r","+- **Decision**: `scripts/verify_commit.py` checks the commit out into a throwaway worktree under the system temp directory and runs the tiers, the four read-only gates and dogfood inside it, then removes the worktree in a `finally` block whether or not a gate failed. The secret scan reads the commit range, not the tree (ADR-145). PRINCIPLE-018 R7 requires it after each commit and before R4's push, so a bad commit is caught while R5's `git reset --soft HEAD^` still applies and the pushed history stays green for `git bisect`.\r","+- **Consequences**: About 15 seconds per commit (measured 14.5s), outside both test tiers. Writing it surfaced two real defects in itself: the first draft returned a bare SHA when no upstream resolved, and `git log -p <sha>` walks every commit reachable from it, so the scan covered the whole history and failed over the already-revoked key of ADR-133; this repository hit that because `@{u}` resolves as a name while `origin/main` has no local ref. `scanned_range` now returns `upstream..head`, else `parent..head`, and a bare SHA only for a root commit. The kit's own citation gate then refused the first commit of this work because the code cited R7 before R7 existed, which is why the rule and the script land together.\r","+- Cross-principle check: PRINCIPLE-001 (no conflict), PRINCIPLE-002 (no conflict), PRINCIPLE-003 (no conflict), PRINCIPLE-006 (no conflict), PRINCIPLE-007 (no conflict), PRINCIPLE-008 (no conflict), PRINCIPLE-010 (one extra ~15s run per commit, outside both test tiers; no conflict), PRINCIPLE-011 (R8 projects keep `aikit check --strict` as their equivalent; no conflict), PRINCIPLE-015 (R4 the worktree lives in the system temp directory, never in the repository), PRINCIPLE-016 (no conflict), PRINCIPLE-017 (no conflict), PRINCIPLE-018 (R7 added; R3 unchanged, R4's push now waits on it, R5 is the stated undo), PRINCIPLE-019 (the scan covers the commits the push would upload (ADR-145); no conflict).\r"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\knowledge\\services.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":16,"oldLines":6,"newStart":16,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | `check_project_hygiene.py` | Scans a project's Python source and static assets: shell/system/exec, non-portable subprocess, unencoded `open()`, any `except` that only discards the error, absolute paths, third-party asset URLs | exit 1 on a finding; built into `aikit check` (ADR-137) |\r"," | `project_publish.py` | Uploads a project's commits to its own GitHub repository (`gh repo create --private --source --remote origin --push`, or a push to an existing `origin`) and auto-pushes after a passing `aikit check`; both first scan exactly the commits they push (`check_secrets.py --commits`: the whole history for a new remote, `@{u}..HEAD` after) and refuse on a finding | `aikit publish` exits 1 on a refusal (ADR-134, ADR-145) |\r"," | `subagent_delegate.py` | Runs one OpenCode sub-agent (roles = `.opencode/agents/*.md`) supervised, stdin closed, with a timeout; reports a ledger changed during the run | `aikit delegate` exits 1 on timeout or a changed ledger (ADR-128) |\r","+| `verify_commit.py` | Checks a commit out into a throwaway worktree and runs the whole gate set there, so a commit that cannot stand alone is caught while it is still local | exit 1 on any failed gate, naming `git reset --soft HEAD^` (PRINCIPLE-018 R7, ADR-149) |\r"," | `dogfood.py` | Runs AIKit's CLIs as real processes in a sandbox: golden path, chaos, gates, `--help` budget | exit 1 on any failed track (PRINCIPLE-015) |\r"," \r"," ## 📋 Design Rules\r"]}]}],"moreFiles":1,"changedFiles":["C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\GUIDELINES.md","C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\README.md","C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\knowledge\\codebase_map.md","C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\knowledge\\decisions.md","C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\knowledge\\services.md","C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\tests\\test_kit.py"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"716bab15-b9a8-4f8f-bdc3-708e21d2256e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit","root":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":3,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Aegean-E/AIKit","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Aegean-E/AIKit","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Aegean-E/AIKit","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ae738072-b177-473b-8e00-23cbd1053625","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit","sessionId":"07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f","version":"2.1.302","gitBranch":"main","slug":"eager-humming-wave"}
