{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f","hash":"397ddcbc5061bb3650c3c2abaf332121446cf8b42d07aa1345c1806befba3bfd","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018W3V86K5EFpJEuJhapY9kG","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:/Users/YUNUS-~1/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit/07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f/scratchpad/v_rule.py","content":"\"\"\"PRINCIPLE-018 R7, its pin, the docs and ADR-149.\"\"\"\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n\ndef edit(path, pairs):\n    p = Path(path)\n    s = p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    for old, new in pairs:\n        assert s.count(old) == 1, (path, old[:70], s.count(old))\n        s = s.replace(old, new)\n    p.write_text(s, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n\nR7 = (\n    \"  7. **Post-Commit Verification of the Delivered Commit** *[Agent]*: After each commit, and \"\n    \"before R4's push, the agent runs `python scripts/verify_commit.py`; the push follows only when \"\n    \"it exits 0. It checks the commit out into a throwaway worktree and runs R3's gates against that \"\n    \"commit alone, because R3 proves the working tree is green and the commit is a different tree \"\n    \"whenever staging is a subset of it (R2). On a failure the agent undoes the still-unpushed commit \"\n    \"with R5's `git reset --soft HEAD^`, adds what the commit lacked, and commits again. A project's \"\n    \"commits are verified by `python aikit.py check --strict <name>` instead (PRINCIPLE-011 R8).\\n\"\n)\n\nguidelines = Path(\"GUIDELINES.md\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\nanchor = guidelines.index(\"  6. **Terse Delivery Confirmation**\")\nend = guidelines.index(\"\\n\", anchor) + 1\nPath(\"GUIDELINES.md\").write_text(guidelines[:end] + R7 + guidelines[end:], encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\nedit(\"GUIDELINES.md\", [\n    (\"pre-commit delivery triad (tests, read-only gates, staged diff); non-destructive recoil.\",\n     \"pre-commit delivery triad (tests, read-only gates, staged diff); the commit itself verified \"\n     \"before the push (`verify_commit.py`); non-destructive recoil.\"),\n])\n\nedit(\"tests/test_kit.py\", [\n    ('        \"PRINCIPLE-018\": {\\n            \"rules\": 6,\\n            \"present\": [\\n',\n     '        \"PRINCIPLE-018\": {\\n            \"rules\": 7,\\n            \"present\": [\\n'\n     '                # ADR-149: the commit is verified on its own before it is pushed.\\n'\n     '                \"the agent runs `python scripts/verify_commit.py`; the push follows only when it exits 0\",\\n'\n     '                \"the commit is a different tree whenever staging is a subset of it\",\\n'),\n])\n\nedit(\"README.md\", [\n    (\"| **Reachability Shield** |\",\n     \"| **Verify the Commit Itself** | `python scripts/verify_commit.py` | Runs every gate against the \"\n     \"commit alone in a throwaway worktree; exits 1 when the commit holds less than the tree it was \"\n     \"tested in (PRINCIPLE-018 R7) |\\n| **Reachability Shield** |\"),\n])\n\nedit(\"knowledge/services.md\", [\n    (\"| `dogfood.py` |\",\n     \"| `verify_commit.py` | Checks a commit out into a throwaway worktree and runs the whole gate set \"\n     \"there, so a commit that cannot stand alone is caught while it is still local | exit 1 on any failed \"\n     \"gate, naming `git reset --soft HEAD^` (PRINCIPLE-018 R7, ADR-149) |\\n| `dogfood.py` |\"),\n])\n\nciting = subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"scripts/sync_principles.py\", \"--citing\", \"PRINCIPLE-018\"],\n                        capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=60, check=True).stdout.split()\nnotes = {\n    \"PRINCIPLE-018\": \"R7 added; R3 unchanged, R4's push now waits on it, R5 is the stated undo\",\n    \"PRINCIPLE-011\": \"R8 projects keep `aikit check --strict` as their equivalent; no conflict\",\n    \"PRINCIPLE-014\": \"the gate runs the same tiers R3 names, in a clean checkout; no conflict\",\n    \"PRINCIPLE-015\": \"R4 the worktree lives in the system temp directory, never in the repository\",\n    \"PRINCIPLE-019\": \"the scan covers the commits the push would upload (ADR-145); no conflict\",\n    \"PRINCIPLE-010\": \"one extra ~15s run per commit, outside both test tiers; no conflict\",\n}\nparts = [f\"{pid} ({notes.get(pid, 'no conflict')})\" for pid in sorted(set(citing) | {\"PRINCIPLE-018\"})]\n\nadr = f\"\"\"\n### ADR-149: The Commit Is Verified On Its Own Before It Is Pushed\n- **Date**: 2026-10-19\n- **Status**: Accepted\n- **Context**: PRINCIPLE-018 R3 runs the delivery triad against the working tree. Under R2's explicit staging the commit is a *different* tree whenever staging is a subset, and nothing checked that one. Both failure modes happened on 2026-10-19: ADR-145 was committed while its implementation sat unstaged, and a stale `codebase_map.md` was committed twice, each time caught only by the next run. Projects already had `aikit check --strict` (ADR-142); AIKit's own commits had no equivalent.\n- **Decision**: `scripts/verify_commit.py` checks the commit out into a throwaway worktree under the system temp directory and runs the tiers, the four read-only gates and dogfood inside it, then removes the worktree in a `finally` block whether or not a gate failed. The secret scan reads the commit range, not the tree (ADR-145). PRINCIPLE-018 R7 requires it after each commit and before R4's push, so a bad commit is caught while R5's `git reset --soft HEAD^` still applies and the pushed history stays green for `git bisect`.\n- **Consequences**: About 15 seconds per commit (measured 14.5s), outside both test tiers. Writing it surfaced two real defects in itself: the first draft returned a bare SHA when no upstream resolved, and `git log -p <sha>` walks every commit reachable from it, so the scan covered the whole history and failed over the already-revoked key of ADR-133; this repository hit that because `@{{u}}` resolves as a name while `origin/main` has no local ref. `scanned_range` now returns `upstream..head`, else `parent..head`, and a bare SHA only for a root commit. The kit's own citation gate then refused the first commit of this work because the code cited R7 before R7 existed, which is why the rule and the script land together.\n- Cross-principle check: {\", \".join(parts)}.\n\"\"\"\nd = Path(\"knowledge/decisions.md\")\nd.write_text(d.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").rstrip(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\" + adr, encoding=\"utf-8\")\nprint(\"ok\", sorted(citing))\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017yeac9eJnVmWzUiTLw5fXN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit && py \"C:/Users/YUNUS-~1/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit/07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f/scratchpad/v_rule.py\" && py scripts/sync_principles.py 2>&1 | grep -iE \"updated|error|exceed|headroom\" | head -4; py scripts/update_knowledge_base.py >/dev/null 2>&1; py scripts/check_test_budgets.py 2>&1 | grep -E \"PASS|FAIL|OK\\]\"","description":"Add R7, pin, docs, ADR-149; sync and run tiers","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
