 delivery triad (tests, gates, diff); each commit verified alone pre-push (R7)\"\nassert s.count(old) == 1\np.write_text(s.replace(old, new), encoding=\"utf-8\")\nPYEOF\npy scripts/sync_principles.py 2>&1 | grep -iE \"ERROR|HEADROOM|synchronized\" | head -2","description":"Trim one more token; check budget","timeout":200000}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_012gbvdP8LN9rHP1oZ8BLsNx":{"cwd":"/c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"df111316-508e-4e0d-ae17-52497623a43f","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgBrvFL2HK77M7ZkgBYuJ","requestRef":"f2a6da94-83ec-4653-b51c-4b4a3b0ea1dd","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1cbb1046-54a9-4620-b63c-2481f1c6bf1b","timestamp":"2026-10-19T15:50:39.154Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit","sessionId":"07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f","version":"2.1.302","gitBranch":"main","slug":"eager-humming-wave"}
{"parentUuid":"1cbb1046-54a9-4620-b63c-2481f1c6bf1b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c3602802-0490-4257-a831-b5d201a35c9d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012gbvdP8LN9rHP1oZ8BLsNx","type":"tool_result","content":"All 8 AI guideline targets and the README principle table are synchronized successfully (9 file(s) updated).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b288d47d-f924-4b79-9d31-cd47d07590a2","timestamp":"2026-10-19T15:50:40.520Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"All 8 AI guideline targets and the README principle table are synchronized successfully (9 file(s) updated).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\.agents\\rules\\principles.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":26,"newStart":1,"newLines":26,"lines":["-# Workspace Agent Rules (Tier 1)","-","-> Generated from `GUIDELINES.md` by `scripts/sync_principles.py`; do not edit.","-> Capsules bind; `GUIDELINES.md` wins on conflict. On a contract change, failure or ambiguity, read the `### PRINCIPLE-NNN:` section of each principle `sync_principles.py --involved` lists; never the whole file unless asked.","-","-## Core Principles","-- PRINCIPLE-000 Meta-Principle Integrity & Mutual Alignment: Every rule binds; conflicts follow R6 order; rule edits re-check every citing principle; gaming a gate is a violation; quality doubts go to the user.","-- PRINCIPLE-001 Progressive Rule Disclosure & Governance Frugality: Pre-Flight checklist before the first Track C edit; Post-Flight checklist before any Track B or C commit; report only failed items (R8).","-- PRINCIPLE-002 Lifecycle-Aligned Instruction Ordering & Attentional Priming: Track via `disruption_recovery.py --track` (A none, B docs/comments but not rule files, C rest); urgency alone never skips P018 gates (R5).","-- PRINCIPLE-003 Empirical Grounding & Anti-Hallucination Invariant: Read-before-write slice freshness; `git grep -w -e` call-site check; deps only if declared; platform parity; ask on intent ambiguity; strict AST syntax gate.","-- PRINCIPLE-004 Attentional Drift Prevention & Compaction Resilience: Plan = latest `[1/` Phase 2 `--desc` in `task_ledger.json`; cold start `--resume`; never re-ask recorded answers; ADR before commit; reads/output <=100 lines.","-- PRINCIPLE-005 AI Cold-Start Readiness & Living Documentation: README <=20k chars: prerequisites, test command, tree; user-visible changes update it same commit; `update_knowledge_base.py --check` gates it.","-- PRINCIPLE-006 Incremental Progress Checkpointing & Disruption Recovery: Commit each `[milestone N/M]` once Phase 4 passes; failing work stays uncommitted, described by `--checkpoint`; `--complete` or `--reset` before switching tasks; `--clean` stale `.tmp_*`.","-- PRINCIPLE-007 Pre-flight Impact & Quality Checklist: Track C first plan checkpoint carries --why --benefits --risks (contract, dependency, concurrency, state) --mitigation; no TODO or stub; no change outside the plan.","-- PRINCIPLE-008 Hierarchical Problem & Task Decomposition: Plan of M<=6 milestones (more: split into tasks), built bottom-up, each passing Phase 4 alone; re-plan = new `[1/M']` checkpoint; sub-agents never write the ledger.","-- PRINCIPLE-009 Modularity & Pluggable Architecture: Every module: no junk-drawer name, roles of 1-5 methods, no import cycle (gated). At a pluggable boundary: 4 layers, registry lookup, constructor DI with default, frozen DTOs.","-- PRINCIPLE-010 Performance & Resource Optimization: Stream uncontrolled input; threads only for steps >=200ms; timeout= on subprocess, with on open(); one fsync per file; `--help` <200ms; unit <=8ms, integ <=200ms/test.","-- PRINCIPLE-011 Zero-Friction Onboarding & Instant Usability: Only declared deps; creates its dirs; prompts only with `--interactive`; no `os.environ[...]` reads; exit 0/1/2; errors give `Why:`/`Fix:`; demo <10s; other software: its `aikit.py` project is the workspace (R8).","-- PRINCIPLE-012 Token Frugality & Lean Code Architecture: LLM code: <=16k-char payloads, static prefix first, schema-checked replies, 429 backoff, step caps; agent: diff -U3, search <=50 hits, relative paths.","-- PRINCIPLE-013 Crash Resilience, State Atomicity & Power-Loss Recovery: State files: >=10MB free, temp + fsync + os.replace (5 tries) + dir fsync, .bak, advisory locking 3s/30s stale, corrupt -> quarantine/.bak/migrate. Generated: temp + fsync + replace.","-- PRINCIPLE-014 Automated Test Verification & Continuous Test Coverage: 100% test pass gate; behaviour change = failing-first test; weakening a test needs user approval + ADR naming it; unit <=8ms/test, no spawns/sleeps; integ <=200ms/test; tempdir + addCleanup; `scripts/check_reachability.py`.","-- PRINCIPLE-015 Universal Operational Dogfooding & Chaos Verification: Domain-specific interactive dogfooding via `scripts/dogfood.py` as a commit gate; golden path + chaos perturbation; non-interactive stdin parity; portable RAII process tree teardown; ephemeral safety jail; terse reporting (<=15 lines).","-- PRINCIPLE-016 AI Knowledge Base & Continuous Synchronization: Canonical `knowledge/` sync; atomic code-and-doc pairing; monotonic append-only ADR register; strict AST syntax validation; link integrity shield; `scripts/update_knowledge_base.py`.","-- PRINCIPLE-017 Living Principles System & Automated Synchronization: Rule sync (`scripts/sync_principles.py`); context budget check; schema compliance; freshness test gate; Tier 1B domain rules (<=1,200 chars).","-- PRINCIPLE-018 Automatic Git Workflow: Automatic conventional commits (`--validate-commit`) + adaptive push, unless the user opts out, never forced; explicit staging (zero `git add .`); pre-commit delivery triad (tests, read-only gates, staged diff); non-destructive recoil.","-- PRINCIPLE-019 Secret & Sensitive Data Hygiene: Zero credentials in tracked files, logs or ledgers; secrets via env/secret store; `.gitignore` credential baseline; `scripts/check_secrets.py` scans staged diffs + ledger; redacted diagnostics; rotate, never revert.","+# Workspace Agent Rules (Tier 1)\r","+\r","+> Generated from `GUIDELINES.md` by `scripts/sync_principles.py`; do not edit.\r","+> Capsules bind; `GUIDELINES.md` wins on conflict. On a contract change, failure or ambiguity, read the `### PRINCIPLE-NNN:` section of each principle `sync_principles.py --involved` lists; never the whole file unless asked.\r","+\r","+## Core Principles\r","+- PRINCIPLE-000 Meta-Principle Integrity & Mutual Alignment: Every rule binds; conflicts follow R6 order; rule edits re-check every citing principle; gaming a gate is a violation; quality doubts go to the user.\r","+- PRINCIPLE-001 Progressive Rule Disclosure & Governance Frugality: Pre-Flight checklist before the first Track C edit; Post-Flight checklist before any Track B or C commit; report only failed items (R8).\r","+- PRINCIPLE-002 Lifecycle-Aligned Instruction Ordering & Attentional Priming: Track via `disruption_recovery.py --track` (A none, B docs/comments but not rule files, C rest); urgency alone never skips P018 gates (R5).\r","+- PRINCIPLE-003 Empirical Grounding & Anti-Hallucination Invariant: Read-before-write slice freshness; `git grep -w -e` call-site check; deps only if declared; platform parity; ask on intent ambiguity; strict AST syntax gate.\r","+- PRINCIPLE-004 Attentional Drift Prevention & Compaction Resilience: Plan = latest `[1/` Phase 2 `--desc` in `task_ledger.json`; cold start `--resume`; never re-ask recorded answers; ADR before commit; reads/output <=100 lines.\r","+- PRINCIPLE-005 AI Cold-Start Readiness & Living Documentation: README <=20k chars: prerequisites, test command, tree; user-visible changes update it same commit; `update_knowledge_base.py --check` gates it.\r","+- PRINCIPLE-006 Incremental Progress Checkpointing & Disruption Recovery: Commit each `[milestone N/M]` once Phase 4 passes; failing work stays uncommitted, described by `--checkpoint`; `--complete` or `--reset` before switching tasks; `--clean` stale `.tmp_*`.\r","+- PRINCIPLE-007 Pre-flight Impact & Quality Checklist: Track C first plan checkpoint carries --why --benefits --risks (contract, dependency, concurrency, state) --mitigation; no TODO or stub; no change outside the plan.\r","+- PRINCIPLE-008 Hierarchical Problem & Task Decomposition: Plan of M<=6 milestones (more: split into tasks), built bottom-up, each passing Phase 4 alone; re-plan = new `[1/M']` checkpoint; sub-agents never write the ledger.\r","+- PRINCIPLE-009 Modularity & Pluggable Architecture: Every module: no junk-drawer name, roles of 1-5 methods, no import cycle (gated). At a pluggable boundary: 4 layers, registry lookup, constructor DI with default, frozen DTOs.\r","+- PRINCIPLE-010 Performance & Resource Optimization: Stream uncontrolled input; threads only for steps >=200ms; timeout= on subprocess, with on open(); one fsync per file; `--help` <200ms; unit <=8ms, integ <=200ms/test.\r","+- PRINCIPLE-011 Zero-Friction Onboarding & Instant Usability: Only declared deps; creates its dirs; prompts only with `--interactive`; no `os.environ[...]` reads; exit 0/1/2; errors give `Why:`/`Fix:`; demo <10s; other software: its `aikit.py` project is the workspace (R8).\r","+- PRINCIPLE-012 Token Frugality & Lean Code Architecture: LLM code: <=16k-char payloads, static prefix first, schema-checked replies, 429 backoff, step caps; agent: diff -U3, search <=50 hits, relative paths.\r","+- PRINCIPLE-013 Crash Resilience, State Atomicity & Power-Loss Recovery: State files: >=10MB free, temp + fsync + os.replace (5 tries) + dir fsync, .bak, advisory locking 3s/30s stale, corrupt -> quarantine/.bak/migrate. Generated: temp + fsync + replace.\r","+- PRINCIPLE-014 Automated Test Verification & Continuous Test Coverage: 100% test pass gate; behaviour change = failing-first test; weakening a test needs user approval + ADR naming it; unit <=8ms/test, no spawns/sleeps; integ <=200ms/test; tempdir + addCleanup; `scripts/check_reachability.py`.\r","+- PRINCIPLE-015 Universal Operational Dogfooding & Chaos Verification: Domain-specific interactive dogfooding via `scripts/dogfood.py` as a commit gate; golden path + chaos perturbation; non-interactive stdin parity; portable RAII process tree teardown; ephemeral safety jail; terse reporting (<=15 lines).\r","+- PRINCIPLE-016 AI Knowledge Base & Continuous Synchronization: Canonical `knowledge/` sync; atomic code-and-doc pairing; monotonic append-only ADR register; strict AST syntax validation; link integrity shield; `scripts/update_knowledge_base.py`.\r","+- PRINCIPLE-017 Living Principles System & Automated Synchronization: Rule sync (`scripts/sync_principles.py`); context budget check; schema compliance; freshness test gate; Tier 1B domain rules (<=1,200 chars).\r","+- PRINCIPLE-018 Automatic Git Workflow: Automatic conventional commits (`--validate-commit`) + adaptive push, never forced; explicit staging (zero `git add .`); pre-commit delivery triad (tests, gates, diff); each commit verified alone pre-push (R7); non-destructive recoil.\r","+- PRINCIPLE-019 Secret & Sensitive Data Hygiene: Zero credentials in tracked files, logs or ledgers; secrets via env/secret store; `.gitignore` credential baseline; `scripts/check_secrets.py` scans staged diffs + ledger; redacted diagnostics; rotate, never revert.\r"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit\\.clinerules","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":26,"newStart":1,"newLines":26,"lines":["-# Cline Rules (Tier 1)","-","-> Generated from `GUIDELINES.md` by `scripts/sync_principles.py`; do not edit.","-> Capsules bind; `GUIDELINES.md` wins on conflict. On a contract change, failure or ambiguity, read the `### PRINCIPLE-NNN:` section of each principle `sync_principles.py --involved` lists; never the whole file unless asked.","-","-## Core Principles","-- PRINCIPLE-000 Meta-Principle Integrity & Mutual Alignment: Every rule binds; conflicts f