{"parentUuid":"45f842cf-1519-43be-8589-313f434dc2e7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgBs155XWa3j8guDR45rK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TuJYAqPHXRMKYZ4nYdwmBr","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:/Users/YUNUS-~1/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit/07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f/scratchpad/v_readme.py","content":"from pathlib import Path\n\np = Path(\"README.md\")\ns = p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n\ndef rep(old, new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old) == 1, old[:70]\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\n\n\n# The new script belongs in the tree the drift shield checks.\nrep(\"│   ├── check_secrets.py                <- Secret & sensitive data scanner (pre-commit gate)\\n\",\n    \"│   ├── check_secrets.py                <- Secret & sensitive data scanner (pre-commit gate)\\n\"\n    \"│   ├── verify_commit.py                <- Verifies a commit alone in a throwaway worktree\\n\")\n\n# Paid for by condensing: the project-memory paragraph repeated what the command matrix states.\nrep(\"A project's memory is its `.aikit/` folder (record, ledger, decisions, guidelines: its own rules, \"\n    \"below the principles), committed in its repository; ledger commands take `--workspace projects/<name>`. \"\n    \"Stack and test command are detected from its files (Python, Node, Rust, Go, Java, .NET); \"\n    \"`--test \\\"<cmd>\\\"` overrides. `check` asks you to record `checklists: passed` or the failed IDs in the \"\n    \"task's latest checkpoint before the commit (PRINCIPLE-001 R8, PRINCIPLE-011 R8); a deliberate hygiene \"\n    \"finding needs `hygiene: allow <reason>` on its own line.\",\n    \"A project's memory is its `.aikit/` folder (record, ledger, decisions, and guidelines: its own rules, \"\n    \"below the principles), committed in its repository; ledger commands take `--workspace projects/<name>`. \"\n    \"Stack and test command are detected from its files (Python, Node, Rust, Go, Java, .NET); \"\n    \"`--test \\\"<cmd>\\\"` overrides. Before a project commit, `check` asks you to record `checklists: passed` \"\n    \"or the failed IDs in the task's latest checkpoint; a deliberate hygiene finding needs \"\n    \"`hygiene: allow <reason>` on its own line.\")\n\nrep(\"**Universal CLI contract (PRINCIPLE-011, PRINCIPLE-015).** Every CLI: `--help`/`-h` prints usage, \"\n    \"writes nothing, exits `0`; exit `0` success, `1` operational failure, `2` misuse (an unknown flag is r\",\n    \"**Universal CLI contract (PRINCIPLE-011, PRINCIPLE-015).** Every CLI: `--help`/`-h` prints usage, \"\n    \"writes nothing, exits `0`; exit `0` success, `1` operational failure, `2` misuse (an unknown flag is r\")\n\np.write_text(s, encoding=\"utf-8\")\nprint(len(s))\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":307,"cache_read_input_tokens":814094,"output_tokens":1316,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":307,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1316,"cache_read_input_tokens":814094,"cache_creation_input_tokens":307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":307},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TuJYAqPHXRMKYZ4nYdwmBr":{"file_path":"C:/Users/YUNUS-~1/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit/07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f/scratchpad/v_readme.py","content":"from pathlib import Path\n\np = Path(\"README.md\")\ns = p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n\ndef rep(old, new):\n    global s\n  