{"parentUuid":"eda57f8c-da0e-4384-96a5-2af4282c948e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgBs6GpbaFjpKnC1etbtH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NFAkENTANaegQkgk4hCYAj","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:/Users/YUNUS-~1/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit/07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f/scratchpad/v_readme2.py","content":"\"\"\"Condense the adopter-copy section: four steps, no capability dropped (ADR-149).\"\"\"\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nNEW = \"\"\"## 📥 Alternative: Copy AIKit Into an Existing Project\n\nThe primary path is above: keep the project under `projects/`. To instead govern a repository in\nplace, copy the source of truth and tooling into it and generate the rest:\n\n```bash\ncd portable_agent_kit\nmkdir -p /path/to/target/.agents\ncp -r GUIDELINES.md scripts knowledge /path/to/target/\ncp -r .agents/rules .agents/skills /path/to/target/.agents/\ncd /path/to/target && python scripts/sync_principles.py && python scripts/update_knowledge_base.py\n```\n\n- **Do not copy** `tests/`, `.github/` or `.agents/task_ledger.json`: they are AIKit's own. The CLI\n  gates in the matrix above carry the enforcement.\n- Replace the copied `knowledge/` documents with your project's, and copy\n  `.agents/rules/readme_quickref.md.template` into your `README.md`, filling every `<FILL` placeholder.\n- If the target already has instruction files, move their project-specific rules into\n  `.agents/rules/domain.md` (max 1,200 chars) and delete the originals. Sync injects that block into\n  all 8 Tier 1 files and refuses to overwrite a hand-authored file (`[PROTECTED]`).\n- The two commands above generate the 8 Tier 1 files (each <=1,600 tokens including Tier 1B) and\n  `knowledge/codebase_map.md`, the AST catalogue of every class, method, argument and docstring.\n\n\"\"\"\n\np = Path(\"README.md\")\ns = p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\nstart = s.index(\"## 📥 Alternative: Copy AIKit Into an Existing Project\")\nend = s.index(\"## 🏛️ The 20 Core Principles\")\n# Keep the horizontal rule that separated the two sections.\ntail = s[start:end]\nrule = \"\\n---\\n\\n\" if tail.rstrip().endswith(\"---\") else \"\\n\"\ns = s[:start] + NEW + rule.lstrip(\"\\n\") + s[end:]\np.write_text(s, encoding=\"utf-8\")\nprint(len(s))\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1864,"cache_read_input_tokens":819648,"output_tokens":1200,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1864,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1200,"cache_read_input_tokens":819648,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1864,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1864},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01NFAkENTANaegQkgk4hCYAj":{"file_path":"C:/Users/YUNUS-~1/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit/07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f/scratchpad/v_readme2.py","content":"\"\"\"Condense the adopter-copy section: four steps, no capability dropped (ADR-149).\"\"\"\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nNEW = \"\"\"## 📥 Alternative: Copy AIKit Into an Existing Project\n\nThe primary path is above: keep the project under `projects/`. To instead govern a repository in\nplace, copy the source of truth and tooling into it and generate the rest:\n\n```bash\ncd portable_agent_kit\nmkdir -p /path/to/target/.agents\ncp -r GUIDELINES.md scripts knowledge /path/to/target/\ncp -r .agents/rules .agents/skills /path/to/target/.agents/\ncd /path/to/target && python scripts/sync_principles.py && python scripts/update_knowledge_base.py\n```\n\n- **Do not copy** `tests/`, `.github/` or `.agents/task_ledger.json`: they are AIKit's own. The CLI\n  gates in the matrix above carry the enforcement.\n- Replace the copied `knowledge/` documents with your project's, and copy\n  `.agents/rules/readme_quickref.md.template` into your `README.md`, filling every `<FILL` placeholder.\n- If the target already has instruction files, move their project-specific rules into\n  `.agents/rules/domain.md` (max 1,200 chars) and delete the originals. Sync injects that block into\n  all 8 Tier 1 files and refuses to overwrite a hand-authored file (`[PROTECTED]`).\n- The two commands above generate the 8 Tier 1 files (each <=1,600 tokens including Tier 1B) and\n  `knowledge/codebase_map.md`, the AST catalogue of every class, method, argument and docstring.\n\n\"\"\"\n\np = Path(\"README.md\")\ns = p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\nstart = s.index(\"## 📥 Alternative: Copy AIKit Into an Existing Project\")\nend = s.index(\"## 🏛️ The 20 Core Principles\")\n# Keep the horizontal rule that separated the two sections.\ntail = s[start:end]\nrule = \"\\n---\\n\\n\" if tail.rstrip().endswith(\"---\") else \"\\n\"\ns = s[:start] + NEW + rule.lstrip(\"\\n\") + s[end:]\np.write_text(s, encoding=\"utf-8\")\nprint(len(s))\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"69261fea-5636-44ce-ba44-3e9cf32ec51a","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgBs6GQ3thrgfizK9A5aY","requestRef":"d8f8ab09-7f7a-4629-9f29-23ac23fcf8af","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8ac75096-c62d-4812-9b29-7d3a0f1522f9","timestamp":"2026-10-19T15:52:52.824Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"C:\\Users\\Yunus-Emre\\Desktop\\portable_agent_kit","sessionId":"07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f","version":"2.1.302","gitBranch":"main","slug":"eager-humming-wave"}
