{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f","hash":"125804ea446db4a8636f5e4880a9d87babe4f4ae20e3b0b4d3b2fb679fdd3cc3","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NFAkENTANaegQkgk4hCYAj","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:/Users/YUNUS-~1/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit/07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f/scratchpad/v_readme2.py","content":"\"\"\"Condense the adopter-copy section: four steps, no capability dropped (ADR-149).\"\"\"\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nNEW = \"\"\"## 📥 Alternative: Copy AIKit Into an Existing Project\n\nThe primary path is above: keep the project under `projects/`. To instead govern a repository in\nplace, copy the source of truth and tooling into it and generate the rest:\n\n```bash\ncd portable_agent_kit\nmkdir -p /path/to/target/.agents\ncp -r GUIDELINES.md scripts knowledge /path/to/target/\ncp -r .agents/rules .agents/skills /path/to/target/.agents/\ncd /path/to/target && python scripts/sync_principles.py && python scripts/update_knowledge_base.py\n```\n\n- **Do not copy** `tests/`, `.github/` or `.agents/task_ledger.json`: they are AIKit's own. The CLI\n  gates in the matrix above carry the enforcement.\n- Replace the copied `knowledge/` documents with your project's, and copy\n  `.agents/rules/readme_quickref.md.template` into your `README.md`, filling every `<FILL` placeholder.\n- If the target already has instruction files, move their project-specific rules into\n  `.agents/rules/domain.md` (max 1,200 chars) and delete the originals. Sync injects that block into\n  all 8 Tier 1 files and refuses to overwrite a hand-authored file (`[PROTECTED]`).\n- The two commands above generate the 8 Tier 1 files (each <=1,600 tokens including Tier 1B) and\n  `knowledge/codebase_map.md`, the AST catalogue of every class, method, argument and docstring.\n\n\"\"\"\n\np = Path(\"README.md\")\ns = p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\nstart = s.index(\"## 📥 Alternative: Copy AIKit Into an Existing Project\")\nend = s.index(\"## 🏛️ The 20 Core Principles\")\n# Keep the horizontal rule that separated the two sections.\ntail = s[start:end]\nrule = \"\\n---\\n\\n\" if tail.rstrip().endswith(\"---\") else \"\\n\"\ns = s[:start] + NEW + rule.lstrip(\"\\n\") + s[end:]\np.write_text(s, encoding=\"utf-8\")\nprint(len(s))\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011ZjRB3xTnGegqMpKKvqW5Y","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /c/Users/Yunus-Emre/Desktop/portable_agent_kit && py \"C:/Users/YUNUS-~1/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/c--Users-Yunus-Emre-Desktop-portable-agent-kit/07a11155-9f67-48dd-9986-2d892e5f4e3f/scratchpad/v_readme2.py\" && py scripts/update_knowledge_base.py --check 2>&1 | grep -iE \"readme\" | head -4","description":"Condense the section; check README","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
