{"parentUuid":"36222ba0-deb8-4732-86fb-d446c086ca4b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgBsAJF2yVkFJVoBhKapf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KrPECVo4KxqzR752NUEw9h","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -q -F - <<'EOF' && git log --oneline -1\nfeat(delivery): verify each commit alone before pushing it\n\nPRINCIPLE-018 R3 runs the delivery triad against the working tree, and\nunder R2's explicit staging the commit is a different tree whenever\nstaging is a subset. Both failure modes happened today: ADR-145 was\ncommitted while its implementation sat unstaged, and a stale codebase\nmap was committed twice. `scripts/verify_commit.py` checks the commit\nout into a throwaway worktree in the system temp directory, runs the\ntiers, the four read-only gates and dogfood inside it, and removes the\nworktree whether or not a gate failed. New R7 requires it after each\ncommit and before R4's push, so a bad commit is caught while R5's\n`git reset --soft HEAD^` still applies (ADR-149).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF","description":"Commit the verifier and R7","timeout":200000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1139,"cache_read_input_tokens":823484,"output_tokens":451,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1139,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":451,"cache_read_input_tokens":823484,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1139,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1139},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_manageme